{"term":"short","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:215751cb88948b2d79","definition":"Having a small distance from one end or edge to another, either horizontally or vertically.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["low","narrow","slim","shallow"],"antonyms":["long","tall","high","broad","deep"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["heightism","pipsqueak","short man syndrome","shortness","shorty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/short#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:819704ac76bba704fb","definition":"Of a person, living being, or object, having a comparatively small height.","example":"Nhung Ngo had the shortest legs at Site-43. She was the shortest member of staff, two inches beneath the positively elfin Delfina Ibanez, and yet Lillian found her inexplicably difficult to shake. Power-walking down the halls didn't do the trick, as it always did when Wettle-dodging, since the diminutive headshrink kept disappearing into commissaries or service corridors or even other people's offices and emerging, smiling, in front of her.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["little","pint-sized","petite","titchy"],"antonyms":["tall"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["heightism","pipsqueak","short man syndrome","shortness","shorty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/short#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:347d654bc0d85829ec","definition":"Having little duration.","example":"Our meeting was a short six minutes today. Every day for the past month it’s been at least twenty minutes long.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["brief","concise"],"antonyms":["long"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["heightism","pipsqueak","short man syndrome","shortness","shorty"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"